    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "ME\nN\nU",
      "MAIN\nMEAL\nENTRÉE\nSPICED CHICKEN ON GARDEN GREENS\nMAIN\nCOURSE\nBEEF TENDERLOIN WITH MADEIRA SAUCE\nGRILLED SALMON WITH CHILLI JAM AND STIR FRIED VEGETABLES\nSALAD OF PRAWNS AND PROSCHITTO\nDESSERT\nMACADAMIA CHEESE CAKE\nSELECTION OF CHEESE AND FRUIT\nCOFFEE TEA HERBAL TEA\nPlease accent our anoloov if vour choice is not wailable\nWINE LIST\nFRENCH CHAMPAGNE\nAUSTRALIAN SPARKING WINE\nAUSTRALIAN VINTAGES\nThe Australian wine industry is one of the most advanced in the world. The first vines were\nplanted in Sydney in 1788, and today, the wines of Australia are internationally recognised and\nEach Australian state has premium wine growing regions,\nSouth Australia's Coonawarra, Clare and Barossa;\nVictoria's Yarra Valley and Mornington Peninsula;\nMargaret River in Western Australia,\nand the Hunter Valley in New South Wales.\nFrom these and other Australian regions we offer you a selection of the following wines:\nRIESLING\nCharacterised by a highly aromatic, flowery nose, a tangy freshness on the palate with a crisp, clean,\nrefreshing finish.\nCHARDONNAY\nA very full and complex wine, with fresh fruity flavour ranging from green stone fruit to ripe\ntropical fruit.\nATICTDATIAN CorT PEnd\nAustralia makes flavoursome reds of a very good quality, deep in colour, rich tasting and verging on\ngenerous or full-bodied styles.\nPORT\nRich and sweet flavour, a pronounced fruity character with a lingering after taste."
